{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772650859,"nonce":"UqY0QNyK7cjh/QFilNnCS8xL9KI=","title":"auth-merge pre-auth-check incorrectly fails on untracked files","message":"## Problem\nThe pre-auth-check in `mandible auth merge` fails if the main worktree has any untracked files (`??` in git status). The auto-fix runs `git clean -fX` which only removes gitignored files, so non-ignored untracked files always cause failure.\n\n**Why this is wrong:** git merge does not conflict on untracked files unless the incoming branch also contains that file. An untracked file that is not in the incoming branch poses no merge risk.\n\n**Fix:** In the pre-auth-check dirty-tree detection, filter out `??` lines (untracked files) from `git status --porcelain` output and only fail on staged or modified tracked files (M, A, D, R, C lines).\n\n**Status:** Fixed in dotfiles (bin/auth-merge). This issue tracks the fix landing in the standalone Mandible repo.\n\nMigrated from dotfiles issue 3f57688.","files":null}]}